      {
        "id": 164726,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-04T04:27:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My default unlock team is Team Leader Tachyon, Dark Visionary, Argent Adept, Grampa Legacy, and whoever you're unlocking for. &nbsp;Legacy or AA can be substituted for other heroes (Probably Nightmist) if you think that the redirection will be handy, but they'll work fine.</p><p>Once you have Ra completely set up (Barring Solar Flare) use Visionary to determine what is on top of the Villain deck, and once it's something that can kill Ra you can play Solar Flare. &nbsp;Ra should go last so that you can confirm that everything else is set up ahead of time. &nbsp;Don't be afraid to deal damage to Ra yourself. &nbsp;Twist the Ether is excellent here, as it will allow Ra to damage himself through Flesh of the Sun God (and help manage the damage so that you deal yourself the right amount). &nbsp;A judicious Twist the Ether on the highest HP Ennead member can allow Ra to be killed by Sun's Fury or Mass Overheating (as well as boosting the damage to make it easier, and reducing the damage to everyone else in case you want to try winning once Ra is dead)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Make sure that the environment is something harmless that is unlikely to kill Ra unexpectedly.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:45:59.146Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
